    "result_text": "Changing the sheet's today now writes the SNAPSHOT lines, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 acceptance tests.\n\n**What it does:** when today moves to a different date, the app writes one line per person, in the same order as the list:\n`SNAPSHOT sheet=<id> by=<user> name=<name> due-total=<due-total>`\nThe due-total is the one from the day being left, and is `n/a` where that person's due-total is n/a. These lines are written before the new today is saved, so they come before any period auto-close lines and the change's ROLLUP/TOTALS lines.\n\n**How:** I added a step to `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/sheets/{sheetId}/today.POST.yml`, between the existing before-figures step and the step that applies the new date. It calls a new class, `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/rollup/RecordSnapshot.java`, which uses the figures already captured before the change, so nothing is worked out twice.\n\nTwo choices of mine you may want to check, since the tests don't cover either:\n- **Same date again:** setting today to the date it already has writes no SNAPSHOT lines, because the request only covers a change of today.\n- **Delegation:** I added SNAPSHOT to the \"figures only\" events in `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/Audit.java`. That means these lines never get the `for=<steward>` ending when someone acts by delegation, the same as ROLLUP, TOTALS and ALERT. If you'd rather they carry it, remove SNAPSHOT from that list.",
